  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Sunday) \nIssued at 1004 PM CST SUN NOV 8 2026\n\nWe are cooling off nicely once again this evening with\ntemperatures already down into the upper 40s to mid 50s. Lows in\nthe mid 30s, light winds, and narrowing dew point depressions\nwill promote another round of patchy frost across the region from\nmidnight through 8 AM Monday morning.\n\nDry air and surface high pressure will keep us dry as we head\nthrough the first half of the work week. The upper level pattern\nstarts to pick up a bit by mid week with a southern stream trough\nlifting across the Southern Plains. Enough moisture looks to pool\nacross the region ahead of this feature to warrant a low to\nmedium (20-40%) chance of rain late Wednesday through Thursday\nmorning. A stronger upper level trough quickly rips across much\nof the eastern US Thursday through the weekend. An associated\ncold front will be sent our way on Thursday with a reinforcing\nsurge of high pressure arriving over the weekend. Limited\nmoisture will lead to a dry FROPA with this late week system.\n\nTemperatures will slowly warm through the work week with highs\nrebounding into the low to mid 70s by Tuesday/Wednesday.\nThursday's cold front will bring another shot of cooler air to\nthe region with highs struggling to break out of the 50s. Lows\nwill plummet into the low to mid 30s next week. Latest NBM\nprobabilities have increased and are now hinting at 60-90% chance\nof seeing freezing temps across our northern counties Saturday\nand Sunday mornings.\n\n95/Castillo",
